# Shell scripts MUST keep LF line endings — they are executed by bash on the
# Linux VM. The Phase 11 ship-out hit a CRLF break (commit dc9a74c "fix CRLF
# on verify script") because verify-phase11.sh was checked out with Windows
# line endings on a fresh clone. Pinning eol=lf prevents the regression for
# verify-phase12.sh and any future *.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Bash-equivalents
*.bash text eol=lf

# The PWA and the extension MUST run the byte-identical Centrifuge build —
# tests/test_pwa_chat.mjs asserts it, because two different realtime client
# builds mean a socket bug reproduces on one surface and not the other. The
# bundle is minified (~8 lines), so core.autocrlf=true silently made the two
# on-disk copies differ by exactly 8 bytes: one path was materialised by a
# checkout (CRLF), the other written by a tool (LF). Pinning eol=lf makes a
# fresh clone produce identical bytes on both paths.
**/vendor/centrifuge.js text eol=lf

# Other infrastructure formats that the Linux VM consumes (avoid surprises)
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
